{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383766-v5-where-to-get-more-information-on-ghouls-in-v5","id":1383766,"title":"[V5] Where to get more information on Ghouls in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-25T07:32:27-07:00","id":1383766,"title":"[V5] Where to get more information on Ghouls in V5?","content":"Clarification: I in two different VTM games one base on V20 Dark Age (Using modified V20 system) and the other using V5 (with some changes).<br /> <br /> So I'm trying to bring my Dark Age V20 character into the modern nights under the V5 system (with my V5 game's ST approval.)<br /> One thing this character has is a ghoul. Well actually ghouls, but some will be retired or just kept in the background to avoid overcrowding. <br /> Some of these ghouls would be hundred of years old and the have followed my character into the modern nights.<br /> <br /> While trying to understand what a ghoul can do, the V20 system seems to have a lot of information on what a ghoul can be like, the lore and the game mechanics. They can get stronger with age, etc. Basically you can make ghoul characters as NPCs to your character or even as characters themselves.<br /> <br /> But, the V5 system (core book) seems to regulate ghouls to just part of 1 page. <br /> <br /> Are there any other books or sources (official preferably) that have more information or resource for how ghouls work in V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T07:34:30-07:00","id":1383768,"title":"","content":"V20's design goals for ghouls is different from V5's design goals for ghouls, at least as far as mechanics go.<br /> <br /> Right now, we only have the one book that details what ghouls do. There are some loresheets about some Revenants in Chicago and Cults, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T12:25:25-07:00","id":1383816,"title":"","content":"That's too bad then. I will have to work something out with my ST then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}